    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nTo reject a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date with a 400, I followed the project's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (mirroring the existing `RequirePostcode` \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` flow):\n\n1. **`RequireNotFutureRegistrationDate.java`** (new function step) \u2014 reads the `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` request; if `registrationDate` is present and `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`, throws the checked exception. Absence is accepted (defaults to server date downstream). It runs on the **raw** supplied value, before `DetermineRegistrationDate` defaults/business-day-adjusts it.\n\n2. **`FutureRegistrationDateException.java`** (new checked exception, `extends Exception`).\n\n3. **`FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds `400` with body `{\"errors\": [\"registrationDate\"]}`, matching the existing handlers' shape.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** `...FutureRegistrationDateException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `futureDate` step between `cityCapacity` and `determineDate`.\n\nThe new acceptance test `errorRejectsFutureDate` (POST owner with `registrationDate: \"2999-01-01\"` \u2192 400) passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
